<title>CYPRUS: OPEC Nov output hit 26.04 mln bpd - MEES.</title>
<headline>OPEC Nov output hit 26.04 mln bpd - MEES.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC crude production surged 400,000 barrels per day (bpd) last month to 26.04 million bpd, the Middle East Economic Survey (MEES) reported on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The OPEC increase was largely attributable to a sharp boost of 312,000 bpd in Iranian output from the low level of 3.443 million bpd registered in October to 3.755 million bpd in November,&quot; the Cyprus-based MEES reported.</p>
<p>OPEC ministers in November agreed to roll-over the group's supply ceiling of 25.033 million bpd.</p>
<p>Venezuela and Qatar also contributed to the surge increasing their output by 100,000 bpd and 20,000 bpd respectively to 3.2 million bpd and 520,000 bpd, both year highs.</p>
<p>Caracas has an OPEC quota of 2.359 million bpd though its oil minister has repeatedly denied Venezuelan overproduction.</p>
<p>MEES assessed Iraqi production unchanged at 550,000 bpd.</p>
</text>
